                <pb facs="0354" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 857.857/102</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 5.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1948. Consul at La Rochelle reports Norwegian steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Girda</hi> bound from Glasgow to La Palice, general cargo, sunk without
                    warning by submarine By gunfire and bombs on 13th instant, about 12 miles from
                    Chassiron Light, He d’Oléron. Two Americans on board, Bryson Georges and Lloyd
                    Cain, one of whom slightly injured in foot; Consul states Americans departed for
                    Marseilles be <pb facs="0355" n="183" xml:id="pg183"/> fore he was able to take
                    depositions. I have telegraphed Consul General at Marseilles to endeavor to find
                    these men and obtain depositions and have instructed Consul at [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">near?</hi>] La Palice to obtain, if possible, needed
                    additional information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
